This pure-R reference implementation uses adaptive summation and analytic
Taylor arithmetic for derivatives. Large-data performance has not been
validated. Extreme means or dispersion can exhaust numerical limits,
which produces an error. Near-deterministic data may not have a finite
dispersion estimate.

Prior weights multiply log likelihood contributions; they do not change
the distribution used by the \code{rd}, \code{qf}, and \code{cdf} callbacks. These
callbacks condition on the fitted mean and dispersion. Probabilities and
quantiles use the numerically truncated distribution; extreme-tail
accuracy is limited by \code{sum_tol}. \code{qf(0, ...)} is zero and \code{qf(1, ...)}
is infinity for positive means. A zero mean is a point mass at zero.

